"Divine Dross is the rotted essence of the would-be god who died ascending at the Black Pyre."
"Dross seeks a body to finish that failed ascension, so it always reaches for a human shape."
"Dross wells up from the burned god's body deep beneath the Black Pyre."
"The god's death loosed the undead curse that raised the Cursed City's folk as skeletons."
"Direct sunlight through an open jar kills Divine Dross within weeks, leaving grey ash."
"A thinking creature taken by Dross keeps its mind for a day, then burns out in rage."
"An intelligent undead, the Cursed City's last high priest, still bottles Dross from the Pyre."
"The high priest sets new jars through the city to breed a host strong enough to hold the god."
"The high priest hides in the tall inner district and sends Night Sentries to guard his jars."
